[Catch2 PATCH] Add file-backed OutputRedirect for crash recovery

Add a process-wide named-file capture mechanism for stdout/stderr,
enabling crash-recovery post-processing that requires the captured
output to outlive the test process. Two new framework CLI flags expose
this:

  --standard-out-redirect-file <path>
  --standard-err-redirect-file <path>

When either flag is set, an OutputRedirectSink is constructed at CLI
parse time and stored in Config. The sink dup2's the named file over the
corresponding file descriptor (1 or 2) for the entire process lifetime,
disables stdio buffering on the source FILE* via setvbuf(_IONBF), and
exposes position-based content reads via getLatestContents() and
getContentsFromPosition(). When the sink is destroyed at process exit,
the original FD target is restored.

The reporter takes ownership of the sinks at reporter-construction time
(see VstestReporter); RunContext consults the sink presence to determine
whether to construct a per-test OutputRedirect (skipped when sinks
active).

Files modified:
  src/catch2/internal/catch_output_redirect.{hpp,cpp}
    - TempFile gains reopen(), getPath(), getContents(int startPosition);
      m_isOwnedTmpFile renamed to m_shouldAutomaticallyDelete; ctor takes
      std::string by value and stores m_filePath
    - New OutputRedirectSink class (process-wide redirect)
    - OutputRedirect refactored to compose two OutputRedirectSink members
      using anonymous tmpfiles (when no process-wide sinks active)

  src/catch2/internal/catch_commandline.cpp
    - Two CLI handlers construct OutputRedirectSink at parse time and
      store raw pointer in Config

  src/catch2/catch_config.{hpp,cpp}
  src/catch2/interfaces/catch_interfaces_config.hpp
    - ConfigData fields and IConfig/Config accessors return
      OutputRedirectSink* (not std::string paths)

  src/catch2/internal/catch_run_context.cpp
    - runCurrentTest skips per-test OutputRedirect when either
      process-wide sink is set; reporter reads sink content via
      position-based getLatestContents() at section traversal completion

The new code is gated on CATCH_CONFIG_EXPERIMENTAL_REDIRECT (which the
SDK defines via target_compile_definitions, and which auto-defines
CATCH_CONFIG_NEW_CAPTURE for the underlying redirect mechanism).
